# R1 through the real play window (W4-WIN-CLOSE C1): the title and the script read one consistent
# state while a publication is held between a turn's outcome record and its snapshot.
# Run by tools/test/viewer_wiring.py; every `expect` fails the session if it is not met.
look 1052 444
key b
select paid
rotate 0
# A first paid build, to have a published outcome that stays shown (the "earlier" control).
click 1052 444
wait outcome
expect outcome Applied
expect published
wait turns 2

# ---- the paid build, held between the record and the swap ---------------------------------------
note money
hold publication
select paid
click 1068 444
wait held
# The window keeps drawing and handling input while the sim thread waits: frames pass, and keys
# rebuild the title inside the interval (the tool's own events, not a refresh helper).
wait frames 5
key n
key p
select paid
wait frames 3
# The script consumer (PlayRunner::feedback in script_tick): the outcome is withheld.
expect outcome Queued
expect published
expect money same
# The title consumer (PlayRunner::feedback in update_title): the receipt is Queued, never Applied.
expect title-lacks Applied
expect title command #2: Queued
checkpoint held_paid
release publication
wait outcome
wait frames 3
expect outcome Applied
expect published
expect money less
expect title command #2: Applied
checkpoint released_paid

# ---- a refusal, held the same way (the sim refuses a second build on the occupied tile) --------
note money
hold publication
click 1068 444
wait held
wait frames 5
key n
key p
select paid
wait frames 3
expect outcome Queued
expect published
expect title-lacks Refused
expect title command #3: Queued
checkpoint held_refused
release publication
wait outcome
wait frames 3
expect outcome Refused Occupied
expect published
expect money same
expect title command #3: Refused (Occupied)
checkpoint released_refused
quit
